    "done_when": "A new module imas_ambix/data/selene_psrc.py is the one SELENE reader §7 names. One public function returns a shot's PSRC record as one frozen value: the boundary above the X-point (surfABVxp, stored in mm and returned in m), the X-point (calRX, calZX), the magnetic axis (calRp0, calZp0) and the plasma current (calIp), each with its time base. Read docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-psrc-selene-inventory.html for each array's shape, unit, time base and layout, including how surfABVxp packs its R and Z vertices and its fill-padded entries; the record drops fill entries and never returns them as vertices. It reads cached channels through imas_alambic.eddb's cache readers, and fetches anything uncached with imas_alambic.eddb.fetch_channels through an extractor the caller supplies. It adds no transport. As §7 states, in packages/imas-alambic/src/imas_alambic/eddb_remote.py both the remote script's _unit inside REMOTE_SCRIPT and the client-side normalise_unit change together: a multi-entry unit list whose entries all agree yields that one unit, and a disagreeing list is still refused. A test in tests/data/test_eddb_cache.py runs both, the script's _unit taken by exec of REMOTE_SCRIPT, over the same agreeing and disagreeing cases. The extractor then serves surfABVxp. A channel that is neither cached nor served raises an error naming the shot and the channel. Tests in tests/data/test_selene_psrc.py use a tmp_path cache seeded by copying the cached 100599 PSRC arrays read-only from /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/100599.zarr (calRX, calZX, calRp0, calZp0, calIp and their time bases), plus a synthetic surfABVxp in mm laid out as the inventory documents, with fill entries. They show four things: the record's boundary is in metres with the fill entries dropped; the axis equals calRp0 and calZp0 at a sample time; a stub extractor serving surfABVxp writes it through fetch_channels and the record then reads it; and a stub extractor that refuses a channel raises an error naming that channel. No test opens ssh. Nothing under /work is written. Write a landing fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-selene-psrc-loader.html. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), run in the foreground and capture once, to a log in the run directory whose first lines give the committed revision the tests ran at and the command, and whose last line is EXIT=: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/data/test_selene_psrc.py tests/data/test_eddb_cache.py; it exits 0, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
